 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Nagiyev is showing his friend Igor around Claude Monet, boasting about everything. He calls the staff by the wrong names and proudly introduces his art director. First, the Russian.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вот, Игорь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это оазис французской кухни.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Анклав качества.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Сколько сил вложено сюда.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Официант, как родной ребенок.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "О, привет, Виляш.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Я Настя, вообще-то.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Новенькая, наверное.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ну, пойдем дальше.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Сделай нам два кофе.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это Виктория Сергеевна.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Арт-директор нашего ресторана.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Добрый день.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Slowly this time.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вот, Игорь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Here you go, Igor.' The small word 'vot' points at the dining room. Igor's name needs no change here.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это оазис французской кухни.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is an oasis of French cuisine.' 'Of French cuisine' has an 'oy' ending on 'French' and an 'i' on 'cuisine'. 'Oasis' is a borrowed word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Анклав качества.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'A bastion of quality.' 'Enclave' is borrowed too. 'Of quality' needs an 'a' ending.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Сколько сил вложено сюда.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'So much effort has gone into this place.' 'How much' is used here as an exclamation. 'Effort' is literally 'strengths'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Официант, как родной ребенок.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'A waiter is like my own child.' 'Own' here means 'by blood', which makes the staff almost family. 'Child' is an irregular word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "О, привет, Виляш.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Oh, hi, Vilyash.' He greets the wrong person with the casual hello. The name he uses is wrong, which is the joke.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Я Настя, вообще-то.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I'm Nastya, actually.' 'Actually' has the little 'to' added, which sharpens the correction. There's no 'am'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Новенькая, наверное.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'She must be new.' 'New girl' is made by adding a small ending to 'new'. 'Probably' is one word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ну, пойдем дальше.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, let's keep going.' 'We'll go' works as 'let's go'. 'Further' is another handy small word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Сделай нам два кофе.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Make us two coffees.' Coffee is masculine and never changes, so 'two' takes its masculine form. 'Make' is the friendly command.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это Виктория Сергеевна.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is Viktoria Sergeyevna.' He gives her first name and patronymic, the formal way. There's no 'is'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Арт-директор нашего ресторана.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The art director of our restaurant.' 'Art director' is a hyphenated compound. 'Of our restaurant' takes an 'ogo' and an 'a'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Добрый день.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Good afternoon.' The greeting means 'kind day'. Vika keeps it short and formal. Let's hear the whole thing again, start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вот, Игорь.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это оазис французской кухни.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Анклав качества.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Сколько сил вложено сюда.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Официант, как родной ребенок.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "О, привет, Виляш.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Я Настя, вообще-то.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Новенькая, наверное.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ну, пойдем дальше.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Сделай нам два кофе.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это Виктория Сергеевна.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Арт-директор нашего ресторана.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Добрый день.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Nagiyev has no idea who half his staff are, but he makes the tour sound grand. 'Voobshche-to' is a handy phrase for 'actually' when you're correcting someone. See you next time!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "До свидания!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
 ],
